# Copy to `.env` and fill it in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so it
# must never hold a real value.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   COOKIE_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
#
# Signs cookies, which is what makes one usable as a session: the client can read
# the value but cannot forge it. `ctx.cookies.signed` throws without it rather
# than quietly writing an unsigned cookie.
#
# Two things about the value:
#
#   Rotating it logs everyone out. Every signed cookie fails verification and
#   reads as absent, which is correct — but it is a deliberate act.
#
#   Every instance needs the same one. A server that invented its own would issue
#   cookies its sibling rejects, and you would see that as random logouts under
#   load rather than as a configuration error. Which is why `npm run dev` is happy
#   to invent one and production refuses to.
COOKIE_SECRET=
